# {{.Title}}

Built with [Aemeath](https://github.com/naufalraism/aemeath).

## Run it

```bash
aemeath dev{{if .Web}} --ts-out web/src/api{{end}}        # the API with hot reload (http://localhost:3000)
go test ./...      # run the tests
```
{{if and .DB (ne .Database "sqlite")}}
The handler tests use a temporary SQLite database. To run them against {{if eq .Database "postgres"}}PostgreSQL{{else}}MySQL{{end}} as well, point `TEST_DATABASE_URL` at a database kept for tests (they add rows to it):

```bash
# macOS, Linux
TEST_DATABASE_URL='{{if eq .Database "postgres"}}postgres://app:app@localhost:5432/app_test?sslmode=disable{{else}}app:app@tcp(localhost:3306)/app_test{{end}}' go test ./...
```

```powershell
# Windows PowerShell
$env:TEST_DATABASE_URL = '{{if eq .Database "postgres"}}postgres://app:app@localhost:5432/app_test?sslmode=disable{{else}}app:app@tcp(localhost:3306)/app_test{{end}}'; go test ./...
```
{{end}}{{if .Web}}
The React app lives in `web/`. In a second terminal:

```bash
cd web
npm install
npm run dev        # http://localhost:5173, proxies /api to the Go server
```

`aemeath dev --ts-out web/src/api` rewrites the typed client, the Zod schemas and the React Query hooks in `web/src/api/` every time the Go code changes, so the frontend always matches the API.

For production, `npm run build` in `web/` fills `web/dist`, which the Go server serves at `/`.
{{else}}
- API docs: http://localhost:3000/docs
- Typed TypeScript client: http://localhost:3000/client.ts
{{end}}
## Add more

```bash
aemeath generate api Product{{if .DB}} --db{{end}}   # CRUD handlers + tests, registered in main.go for you
aemeath generate job SendEmail                      # a background job with a retrying runner
aemeath generate docker                             # Dockerfile + docker-compose.yml
aemeath ts --out web/src/api                        # TypeScript client, Zod schemas, React Query hooks
```
{{if .DB}}
{{- if eq .Database "postgres"}}
The database is PostgreSQL. The server reads its connection string from `DATABASE_URL`: copy `.env.example` to `.env`, which `aemeath dev` reads, start a development database with `docker compose up db` (it creates the `app` database), then run `aemeath dev`. Each generated resource creates its own table when the server starts. The generated handler tests use a temporary SQLite file, so they need no server.
{{- else if eq .Database "mysql"}}
The database is MySQL (MariaDB works too). The server reads its connection string from `DATABASE_URL`: copy `.env.example` to `.env`, which `aemeath dev` reads, start a development database with `docker compose up db`, then run `aemeath dev`. Each generated resource creates its own table when the server starts. The generated handler tests use a temporary SQLite file, so they need no server.
{{- else}}
The database is SQLite: the file `app.db` (ignored by git), or the path in `DATABASE_PATH`. In Docker it is `/app/data/app.db`, in a volume that outlives the container. Each generated resource creates its own table when the server starts.
{{- end}}
{{end}}
